    specific technical specialisation, DNA analysis, toxicology, or ballistics, and for moving into
    senior scientific officer or academic roles. Separately, a digital forensics certification (GCFA,
    CHFI, EnCE) can matter a great deal, but it works best when layered on top of real IT or forensic
    fundamentals, aimed specifically at the cyber and digital forensics roles that pay a real premium.
    For a commerce-track student, a Certified Fraud Examiner credential opens forensic accounting work
    without a science lab at all.
  </p>

  <div class="honest-take">
