    <p>
      An M.Sc genuinely helps for a specific specialisation or a move into senior government roles,
      but it rarely changes outcomes much for a graduate who has not yet cleared the actual
      recruitment exam. A digital forensics certification is not a rescue plan for a weak core
      science foundation; it works best when paired with real technical understanding, aimed at the
      fastest-growing corner of the same industry rather than treated as an escape from it.
    </p>
